{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/858243-face-in-the-crowd","id":858243,"title":"Face in the Crowd","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-03T02:46:01-07:00","id":858243,"title":"Face in the Crowd","content":"Hi, I need some clarification about this power. It says:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>&quot;Unless the vampire\u2019s doing something to draw people\u2019s attention \u2014 pulling a gun, or screaming at people \u2014 or he\u2019s in a place where someone doesn\u2019t expect anyone else to be, everyone around him ignores him&quot;.</i> </div> </div> </div>So, if the vampire is getting into, for instance, a nunnery where the nuns are not expecting to find any foreign, should they be able to notice her or the vampire mingles among the sisters?<br /> What are the situation in wich the vampire should be noticed? Just in place where really none should be inside, for example inside a closed museum or an abandoned house, or even in place where common people shouldn't be inside?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T03:16:02-07:00","id":858254,"title":"","content":"It says 'doesnt expect anyone else to be', so by that I believe it means it only kicks in if NOBODY is supposed to be in there beyond that person. Someone living alone would notice you entering their place, for instance, but nuns in a nunnery wouldn't notice you even if you came in brandishing pentagrams.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T03:24:23-07:00","id":858256,"title":"","content":"Ok thanks. It is how I always read it but since my player used it to be unnoticed during a police search warrant, I found it really strong and much like to cloak of shadow and I preferred to ask you for clarification <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T03:47:52-07:00","id":858262,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Face in the Crowd makes people register you as a random dude of no consequence, so it only works when they're expecting to <i>see</i> random dudes of no consequence. Anywhere private and there are no crowds to become a face in.<br /> <br /> It might work during a police raid if he's in a house with a bunch of people. The cops are looking for someone specific, so their eyes will glaze over him and they'll be all &quot;not our dude&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T04:01:44-07:00","id":858266,"title":"","content":"Ok but the point is if the vampire could mingles himself among the cops. I mean, what should alerts the cops? The absence of uniform? I can understand a lonley vigilant searching in an abandoned house but what about a group of people or officer? Why shouldn't the vampire mingles among them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T04:21:45-07:00","id":858272,"title":"","content":"No, I don't think that would work. Too much interaction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T08:52:47-07:00","id":858359,"title":"","content":"I would think that a person with obfuscate can just walk around said police station as There are often lots of people walking around. Cops, lawyers, random people, criminals. But Should you start talking to someone specific, that draws their attention to you. Which then might lead that one person to question why you are there. <br /> <br /> The police raid of a house full of other people, I agree that they would look you over and think you werent the guy. Unless you went to speak to one of them. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T09:29:44-07:00","id":858369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/858243-face-in-the-crowd?p=858266#post858266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok but the point is if the vampire could mingles himself among the cops. I mean, what should alerts the cops? The absence of uniform? I can understand a lonley vigilant searching in an abandoned house but what about a group of people or officer? Why shouldn't the vampire mingles among them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Face in the Crowd doesn't allow you to be seen as a specific kind of person (that's what Familiar Stranger is for), it just makes you seem like a random passerby of no importance. So, it wouldn't really allow you to mingle with a group of cops. For one thing, the cops wouldn't percieve you as one of them, just as some random person, and once they question what this random person is doing here, that will break the Obfuscate effect. The other thing is, mingling would require you to interact, which would call attention to yourself and break the Obfuscate effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T09:54:54-07:00","id":858379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/858243-face-in-the-crowd?p=858266#post858266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok but the point is if the vampire could mingles himself among the cops. I mean, what should alerts the cops? The absence of uniform? I can understand a lonley vigilant searching in an abandoned house but what about a group of people or officer? Why shouldn't the vampire mingles among them?</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's while executing a search warrant? It literally depends on the scenario, I wouldn't be inclined to think it would work because the police would know by sight who their co-workers are, and in the event of a raid (which is usually planned) they ARE going to know who regulars/frequent visitors are. If it's a case of a spontaneous public disturbance and police are called in and it escalates, then they may be able to slip away unnoticed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T10:08:00-07:00","id":858387,"title":"","content":"Ok I think to understand now <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Thank you all <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T14:43:33-07:00","id":858535,"title":"","content":"I think we are forgetting the rest of the text.<br /> <br /> For the rest of the scene, p<b>eople\u2019s eyes just slide off the<br /> vampire.</b> <b>People can tell that someone\u2019s there, but they don\u2019t<br /> remember who he is or what he looks like; he\u2019s just \u201csome guy,\u201d</b><br /> average height and build, average hair, average clothes. Unless<br /> the vampire\u2019s doing something to draw people\u2019s attention \u2014<br /> pulling a gun, or screaming at people \u2014 or he\u2019s in a place where<br /> someone doesn\u2019t expect anyone else to be, everyone around him<br /> ignores him. They don\u2019t care what he\u2019s carrying; he could walk<br /> down the street with an assault rifle strapped across his back<br /> or a body slung over his shoulder, and as long as he doesn\u2019t use<br /> it to draw attention, <b>nobody particularly cares or remembers. </b><br /> <br /> <br /> This discipline literally makes people not be able to notice you. Have you ever been in a store and someone was shouting your name, but they have to run up to you and touch you before you notice? Have you ever been in the break room and your coworker comes in grabs a soda and leaves but you just cant remember who it was because you didnt look up from your book or you were talking to someone else? Or you are walking past the office and Bob is talking to ... Someone but you just dont notice or care to notice. You just keep doing your own thing and move on.<br /> <br /> <br /> If the vampire is violent towards someone \u2014 if he punches<br /> someone or starts feeding in a crowded subway station \u2014 his<br /> victim will automatically notice. <b>If he\u2019s doing something that<br /> would draw attention, including but not limited to being violent,<br /> everyone around him must make a reflexive Wits + Composure<br /> roll to notice the commotion,</b> penalized by the vampire\u2019s<br /> Obfuscate dots. The vampire\u2019s predatory aura seemingly<br /> disappears, so that other vampires can\u2019t sense it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T15:31:54-07:00","id":858561,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but being some nondescript person somewhere where nondescript people aren't supposed to be would in and of itself draw attention and break the effect. If cops are the only people who are supposed to be there, no one is going to be able to dismiss &quot;some guy, probably not important&quot; because unimportant people aren't supposed to be there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T15:38:01-07:00","id":858568,"title":"","content":"Imagine the cops are a bunch of PCs. You couldn't slip a vampire in there, could you? So it doesn't work on NPCs either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T16:01:54-07:00","id":858578,"title":"","content":"Then how could you walk around a bus station carrying corpse and have no one notice you? <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Or how could you walk in a school parking lot carrying an assault rifle and have no one notice you?<br /> <br /> I feel like being in a crack house that is getting raided and having no one notice you is right on par with the examples given.<br /> <br /> Sure if 4 people are suppose to be in your pc's car and suddenly there is a 5th. I think there is a problem.<br /> <br /> Another example. A school. only students and the teachers are suppose to be there. But how often do you notice the repair man or the delivery man? Or the parent dropping off something for a student or the mail man? Or the substitute you haven't seen before?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 04-03-2016, 07:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T16:08:27-07:00","id":858585,"title":"","content":"Because a bus station and a school are both places where you would expect to see &quot;I dunno, some dude. I didn't really pay much attention to him.&quot; A crack den might also be. A crack den in the middle of a police raid is not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 04-03-2016, 07:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T16:25:00-07:00","id":858592,"title":"","content":"There is another thread about this about walking around in a military base. I believe they said that would fly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 04-03-2016, 07:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T17:19:05-07:00","id":858619,"title":"","content":"If &quot;some guy/gal&quot; would not attract attention simply by virtue of being there being &quot;just a guy/gal&quot;, Face in the Crowd should work.<br /> <br /> It would work in a nunnery, assuming that you are NOT brandishing pentagrams (mostly for the &quot;brandishing&quot; part, you could have one painted on your face or something I suppose); but not in any situation in which any on the nuns would look at her sisters in the room and identify them all at a glance, because a that point they would go &quot;well here we are for our turn in the kitchen, sister Mary, sister Clara, sister Madeline, sister SomeGal and me WAIT WHAT!?!&quot;.<br /> <br /> Another example. If Mr. Iam A. Touchstone and his 2 roommates invite to a party at their house 7 people each, many of which don't know each other, Iam's (un)dead Nosferatu cousin could easily slip inside by activating Face in the Crowd and nobody would notice there are 25 people instead of 24. He's somebody else's friend.<br /> <br /> If Iam invites five close friends for a fairly quiet poker night/ RPG session, on the other hand, his (un)dead Nosferatu cousin can't just stay in the room with them and make them believe he's &quot;some player/gamer&quot;. There shouldn't be any &quot;some guy&quot; there, so he can't make them think he's one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1866-ophion","name":"Ophion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T23:38:08-07:00","id":858793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/858243-face-in-the-crowd?p=858619#post858619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another example. If Mr. Iam A. Touchstone and his 2 roommates invite to a party at their house 7 people each, many of which don't know each other, Iam's (un)dead Nosferatu cousin could easily slip inside by activating Face in the Crowd and nobody would notice there are 25 people instead of 24. He's somebody else's friend.<br /> <br /> If Iam invites five close friends for a fairly quiet poker night/ RPG session, on the other hand, his (un)dead Nosferatu cousin can't just stay in the room with them and make them believe he's &quot;some player/gamer&quot;. There shouldn't be any &quot;some guy&quot; there, so he can't make them think he's one.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I actually once ran with something between these examples; a single Obfuscate user carefully negotiating a houseful of disparate family members during Thanksgiving. <br /> <br /> The Obfuscate user was assumed to be just some relative who the victim wasn't very familiar with, unless direct observation or interaction was attempted. In a setting so intimate, getting the attention of a single person was immediately hazardous, but as long as you could skirt the edges of groups, keep moving purposefully long enough to avoid polite conversation, and avoid &quot;look at us here all together, isn't this nice&quot; moments, it was possible to dance from one side of the house to the other.<br /> <br /> <i>I</i> believe I handled it properly, but I'm certainly open to correction. I prefer to stay as RAW as I can with Disciplines.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T23:52:54-07:00","id":858797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hastur00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/858243-face-in-the-crowd?p=858793#post858793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I actually once ran with something between these examples; a single Obfuscate user carefully negotiating a houseful of disparate family members during Thanksgiving. <br /> <br /> The Obfuscate user was assumed to be just some relative who the victim wasn't very familiar with, unless direct observation or interaction was attempted. In a setting so intimate, getting the attention of a single person was immediately hazardous, but as long as you could skirt the edges of groups, keep moving purposefully long enough to avoid polite conversation, and avoid &quot;look at us here all together, isn't this nice&quot; moments, it was possible to dance from one side of the house to the other.<br /> <br /> <i>I</i> believe I handled it properly, but I'm certainly open to correction. I prefer to stay as RAW as I can with Disciplines.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds pretty much like how I would have run such a scene as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T10:32:57-07:00","id":859108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hastur00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/858243-face-in-the-crowd?p=858793#post858793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually once ran with something between these examples; a single Obfuscate user carefully negotiating a houseful of disparate family members during Thanksgiving.<br /> <br /> The Obfuscate user was assumed to be just some relative who the victim wasn't very familiar with, unless direct observation or interaction was attempted. In a setting so intimate, getting the attention of a single person was immediately hazardous, but as long as you could skirt the edges of groups, keep moving purposefully long enough to avoid polite conversation, and avoid &quot;look at us here all together, isn't this nice&quot; moments, it was possible to dance from one side of the house to the other.<br /> <br /> <i>I</i> believe I handled it properly, but I'm certainly open to correction. I prefer to stay as RAW as I can with Disciplines.[/SIZE][/FONT][/COLOR]</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/858243-face-in-the-crowd?p=858619#post858619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If &quot;some guy/gal&quot; would not attract attention simply by virtue of being there being &quot;just a guy/gal&quot;, Face in the Crowd should work.<br /> <br /> It would work in a nunnery, assuming that you are NOT brandishing pentagrams (mostly for the &quot;brandishing&quot; part, you could have one painted on your face or something I suppose); but not in any situation in which any on the nuns would look at her sisters in the room and identify them all at a glance, because a that point they would go &quot;well here we are for our turn in the kitchen, sister Mary, sister Clara, sister Madeline, sister SomeGal and me WAIT WHAT!?!&quot;.<br /> <br /> Another example. If Mr. Iam A. Touchstone and his 2 roommates invite to a party at their house 7 people each, many of which don't know each other, Iam's (un)dead Nosferatu cousin could easily slip inside by activating Face in the Crowd and nobody would notice there are 25 people instead of 24. He's somebody else's friend.<br /> <br /> If Iam invites five close friends for a fairly quiet poker night/ RPG session, on the other hand, his (un)dead Nosferatu cousin can't just stay in the room with them and make them believe he's &quot;some player/gamer&quot;. There shouldn't be any &quot;some guy&quot; there, so he can't make them think he's one.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I mostly agree with you ... Well with you both here. I think that given many scenarios we would come up with the same Answer/ruling. <br /> <br /> Hatsur00 I would have done the same for the family only event. And the nunnery too as long as you weren't wielding the pentagram as a weapon. <br /> <br /> obfuscate as written says it ignores the person.. not makes you notice them as some guy/gal. it makes them UNNOTICED. your eyes literally slide off and you cant remember who it was later. So I believe the kitchen scene in the nunnery would be more like. &quot;Come on Clara and Madeline, let's do the dishes.&quot; you note that &quot;somegal&quot; is there but they are too unimportant to include in your task of doing the dishes for kitchen duty and too unimportant for you to want to speak to them. just a body in the room that will move on. as long as it is expected that it is normal for people to be moving in and out of the kitchen while you are there. But that would change if you said. Clara Madeline and Mary are the only ones to be in the kitchen at this time, everyone else go Here. Then a 4th body would be drawing attention by being there. <br /> <br /> like a military base or a police station that people will be moving around and that perhaps not everyone knows everyone's name. Even so there could be that new guy, but the power literally states it makes the others IGNORE YOU not that it turns you into &quot;some guy&quot;. They barely register at all. so Nos. might be the only one walking down the street in a military base, but it is perfectly normal to be the only one walking down and when asked about it later, you cant remember what they looked like or any details about what they were or were not wearing. Likely if it was even a boy or a girl. <br /> <br /> I agree with not the poker party because it is invite only and no one else is expected to be there in a private location. <br /> <br /> So my point is that, It doesnt turn you into &quot;some guy/gal&quot;... it makes it so viewers dont even spend a fraction of a moment trying to figure out if that is random joe or jane, they ignore you like you arent even there. <br /> <br /> I think we view it slightly different, which is entirely ok to interpret texts different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T10:41:31-07:00","id":859109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/858243-face-in-the-crowd?p=859108#post859108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> obfuscate as written says it ignores the person.. not makes you notice them as some guy/gal.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is, in fact, <i>exactly </i>what it says. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> People can tell that someone\u2019s there, but they don\u2019t remember who he is or what he looks like; he\u2019s just \u201csome guy,\u201d </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T10:51:25-07:00","id":859113,"title":"","content":"I think we're arguing over whether the vampire is &quot;just some guy&quot; because the power makes you ignore them, or if you ignore the vampire because the power makes them &quot;just some guy&quot;. Seems like a distinction without difference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T10:57:57-07:00","id":859118,"title":"","content":"I think the contention is more about what &quot;just some person&quot; entails. I personally agree with Vitalis, in that it suits the situation. In the nunnery kitchen, you're &quot;Just some person that works in the nunnery kitchen&quot;, pentagrams or not, but in the private card game, you can't be &quot;Just some close friend I invited&quot;, because that distinction is kinda silly to go through someone's head.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T12:49:53-07:00","id":859181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/858243-face-in-the-crowd?p=859118#post859118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the contention is more about what &amp;quot;just some person&amp;quot; entails. I personally agree with Vitalis, in that it suits the situation. In the nunnery kitchen, you're &amp;quot;Just some person that works in the nunnery kitchen&amp;quot;, pentagrams or not, but in the private card game, you can't be &amp;quot;Just some close friend I invited&amp;quot;, because that distinction is kinda silly to go through someone's head.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd agree with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T07:12:35-07:00","id":859618,"title":"","content":"As long as we're talking about Face in the Crowd, I'm curious. Most of the discussion seems to be focused on when and where a vampire can be &quot;just some guy&quot;, but what about drawing attention? I mean, I would think walking around with an assault rifle or carrying a body would count as drawing notice, but the write up lists those as examples of things that are fine to do. What, short of violence, would be a good example of &quot;drawing attention&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","name":"Jaerys","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T07:20:29-07:00","id":859627,"title":"","content":"If I'm not wrong, point that rifle to someone is wirte as &quot;drawing attention&quot;. I think every interaction with someone draw his attention on you and threaten him is defintely an interaction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T10:44:16-07:00","id":859742,"title":"","content":"This is not by any means a complete list, but I would say the following would be drawing attention:<br /> <br /> Touching someone. ( like slipping your hand into your boyfriend's or tapping them on the shoulder. )<br /> <br /> Speaking directly to someone ( which would break it for that person )<br /> <br /> Addressing the crowd (which would break it for everyone )<br /> <br /> wielding a weapon(or object) in a threatening manner. ( Walking down the street with the riffle on your back or in your hands, but pointed down would not, but pointing at everyone who walked by, would.)<br /> <br /> Hitting someone.<br /> <br /> Being in a place where no one else is suppose to be. ( Private residence. The president's office. The bank vault. )<br /> <br /> Anything that makes a commotion. ( tripping and falling down the stairs )<br /> <br /> <br /> Otherwise, I believe most everything else you would be totally ignored.<br /> <br /> <br /> Remember when you are breaking it for just that one person or the victim everyone else gets : <br /> <br /> <b><i><b>If he\u2019s doing something that would draw attention, including but not limited to being violent, everyone around him must make a reflexive Wits + Composure roll to notice the commotion,</b> penalized by the vampire\u2019s Obfuscate dots</i></b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 04-05-2016, 01:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T11:15:00-07:00","id":859763,"title":"","content":"What if the vampire is using mundane stealth or larceny at the time? Does a Nosferatu pick pocket have to worry about being caught because they are &quot;touching someone&quot;? If so, would Face in the Crowd's penalty to perception checks apply? What if the Nosferatu was sneaking up on someone to stab them in a crowd? It's clear the bystanders would suffer a penalty to their perception check to notice the attack, but what about the victim? Would Face in the Crowd have any impact on the chance of noticing the ambush?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3755,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","user":"Jaerys","date":". 04-05-2016, 02:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","name":"Jaerys","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T11:17:43-07:00","id":859767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jaerys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/858243-face-in-the-crowd?p=859763#post859763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if the vampire is using mundane stealth or larceny at the time? Does a Nosferatu pick pocket have to worry about being caught because they are &quot;touching someone? If so, would Face in the Crowd's penalty to perception checks apply? What if the Nosferatu was sneaking up on someone to stab them in a crowd? It's clear the bystanders would suffer a penalty to their perception check to notice the attack, but what about the victim? Would Face in the Crowd have any impact on the chance of noticing the ambush?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say in the case of mundane stealth added in, you just compare that to the Wits + Composure - Obfuscate roll everyone gets; they have to actually beat you, rather than just getting a basic success. The target, meanwhile, would make the normal ambush roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T11:21:08-07:00","id":859771,"title":"","content":"I would rule that if you have obfuscate on and are planning on stabbing someone. It would cause the roll when you actually did the stabbing. Mainly, because you wouldnt be walking around with the knife up in the air all Psycho style all the way over to the person. It would be safe to assume that you'd keep it hidden and pull it from a hidden spot.<br /> <br /> As far as pick pocketing. if you were successful the victim wouldn't get to roll. as in that scenario you are purposely trying NOT to draw attention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T11:39:29-07:00","id":859782,"title":"","content":"Sleight of Hand is normally a contested action vs the opponents Wits + Composure/Larceny. Would Face in the Crowd penalize the pick pocket target's roll or not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","name":"Jaerys","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T11:46:38-07:00","id":859786,"title":"","content":"By RAW, I'd say no, because as soon as you make them the target they have a normal chance to spot you, as stealing draws attention, so they get a normal roll to see. On the other hand, I could easily see it house ruled that it does at least cause a penalty since you aren't inherently drawing attention unless you're caught.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T12:16:32-07:00","id":859805,"title":"","content":"Well, doing something that draws attention forces a Perception check penalized by your dots in Obfuscate. If they fail that, you might apply a contextual modifier to their ability to notice you pickpocketing them, or you might rule that you can just do it. Interesting note: One can extrapolate that given situations where you're in a crowd, that stealth automatically succeeds. Doing something that breaks the assumption that you're just another face in the crowd forces that perception check. Sneaking around some place that isn't open to people might qualify, in which case it might be that the first dot applys automatic success in crowds, and a perception malus to stealth in general.<br /> <br /> It would make sense too, as the intermediate step between unmodified stealth and the &quot;I Win&quot; stealth of Obfuscate 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 04-05-2016, 04:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}